# dist/ IS committed — this is a published package, consumers consume the
# pre-built artifacts. Rebuild locally with `pnpm build` after touching
# resources/js/ and commit the dist/ change in the same PR. See SECURITY.md.

# pnpm-workspace.yaml IS committed, but only for the minimumReleaseAge
# supply-chain cooldown — it is the only config source pnpm enforces it
# from (package.json#pnpm tested inert on pnpm 11). NEVER commit
# allowBuilds entries: that would silently grant build-script execution
# to any future CI workflow. Keep build approvals local-only
# (uncommitted working-tree edit) — reviewers must reject any PR that
# adds allowBuilds here.
